   330	    files the root itself introduced (a migration in a repo's FIRST commit was
   331	    never classified at all; probed end-to-end). None baseline means git could
   332	    not answer, or the history is SHALLOW — a shallow boundary looks exactly
   333	    like a root commit to rev-list --max-parents=0, and treating it as one
   334	    silently drops everything at or before the boundary; fail closed and let
   335	    the operator fetch full history (CI: fetch-depth: 0, or pass --base).
