  2231	    reviewer's own last word is the one that counts), and any earlier canonical
  2232	    FAIL still loses — a transcript that says FAIL anywhere and PASS later is
  2233	    exactly the ambiguity this refuses to resolve in the change's favour.
  2234	    Anything that is not byte-for-byte one of the two canonical lines, after
  2235	    trimming surrounding whitespace, is a fail.
