The baseline logic has exposed a merge-blocking authorization flaw: an L3 commit with reviews but no human approval becomes a trusted baseline, so a later L1 commit can make the branch gate at L1 even though merging that branch still includes the unapproved L3 change. I’m now checking adjacent bypasses—transcript requirements, reviewer-command trust, and whether commands can mutate the reviewed tree—and running the available tests/probes.
