The full suite could not execute in this read-only sandbox because 183 tests require writable temporary directories; that is an environment limitation, not a product failure. A pure read-only probe did reproduce one parser bypass: `VERDICT: FAIL`, followed by more than 4 KB, then `VERDICT: PASS` is classified as `pass`. Static inspection has also confirmed several independent fail-open paths.
codex
Merge blocked. These are behavioral/security defects, not style issues.

- **P0 — Human approval can be bypassed through a later low-risk commit.** `_validated_baseline` accepts an unsigned L3 report under verification-only scope and advances the baseline ([bin/coverloop:396](/Users/[REDACTED:user]/protocol-loop/bin/coverloop:396), [bin/coverloop:400](/Users/[REDACTED:user]/protocol-loop/bin/coverloop:400)). Subsequent classification excludes that baseline commit ([bin/coverloop:476](/Users/[REDACTED:user]/protocol-loop/bin/coverloop:476)). The regression test explicitly demonstrates an unapproved migration followed by an L1 commit passing the gate ([tests/test_properties.py:1976](/Users/[REDACTED:user]/protocol-loop/tests/test_properties.py:1976), [tests/test_properties.py:1998](/Users/[REDACTED:user]/protocol-loop/tests/test_properties.py:1998)). Merging the final branch still includes the unapproved migration. A trusted `--base origin/main` avoids this in CI, but default `coverloop check` remains fail-open.

- **P0 — “Verified” baselines do not require transcript-backed reviews.** The baseline call omits `require_captured=True` ([bin/coverloop:396](/Users/[REDACTED:user]/protocol-loop/bin/coverloop:396)); its default is false ([bin/coverloop:1634](/Users/[REDACTED:user]/protocol-loop/bin/coverloop:1634)), so `reviewer_check` accepts self-attested passes ([bin/coverloop:1600](/Users/[REDACTED:user]/protocol-loop/bin/coverloop:1600)). An L3 report created with bare `--codex pass --glm pass` can therefore become a baseline, after which a low-tier commit makes `check` skip both real reviewers.

- **P0 — The repository can still control its reviewer command.** Only the policy file’s location and mode are validated; its command strings are returned unchecked ([bin/coverloop:2298](/Users/[REDACTED:user]/protocol-loop/bin/coverloop:2298)). They are then executed through a shell in the repository ([bin/coverloop:981](/Users/[REDACTED:user]/protocol-loop/bin/coverloop:981)). The tests explicitly configure reviewer executables inside the reviewed repository ([tests/test_properties.py:1853](/Users/[REDACTED:user]/protocol-loop/tests/test_properties.py:1853)). A change can modify such a script to print `VERDICT: PASS`, defeating the stated outside-repository trust boundary.

- **P1 — Tests or reviewers can mutate the artifact after the clean-tree check.** Cleanliness is checked only before commands run ([bin/coverloop:2345](/Users/[REDACTED:user]/protocol-loop/bin/coverloop:2345)). After tests and reviewer commands execute, `check` calls `evaluate` directly ([bin/coverloop:2459](/Users/[REDACTED:user]/protocol-loop/bin/coverloop:2459)); the constructed `require_clean_tree=True` namespace is unused. A test can repair the working tree, test the repaired content, and let `SAFE TO MERGE` approve the faulty committed HEAD.

- **P1 — An earlier canonical failure can be hidden outside the tail window.** `transcript_verdict` scans only the final 4 KB ([bin/coverloop:2227](/Users/[REDACTED:user]/protocol-loop/bin/coverloop:2227), [bin/coverloop:2237](/Users/[REDACTED:user]/protocol-loop/bin/coverloop:2237)). I reproduced that `VERDICT: FAIL`, 5 KB of text, then `VERDICT: PASS` returns `pass`, contradicting the documented “FAIL anywhere” rule.

- **P1 — `check` ignores an attestation failure caused by uncommittable evidence.** `_cmd_attest_locked` returns failure when Git ignores generated evidence ([bin/coverloop:1444](/Users/[REDACTED:user]/protocol-loop/bin/coverloop:1444)), but `cmd_check` stores and ignores that return code ([bin/coverloop:2420](/Users/[REDACTED:user]/protocol-loop/bin/coverloop:2420)). Because the files still exist locally, later validation can print `SAFE TO MERGE` even though the report/transcripts will not enter the PR.

- **P2 — Swapping the configured L2 primary to GLM cannot succeed.** `check` runs the configured primary ([bin/coverloop:2400](/Users/[REDACTED:user]/protocol-loop/bin/coverloop:2400)), but L2 evaluation always requires the fixed `codex` field ([bin/coverloop:1675](/Users/[REDACTED:user]/protocol-loop/bin/coverloop:1675)). This fails closed but contradicts the advertised role configurability.

The full suite was not executable in this read-only sandbox because 183 tests require writable temporary directories. The verdict-window bypass was reproduced with a read-only direct probe.

